# Safe Refactor And Security Baseline

- Refactor in behavior-preserving steps first, then functional improvements.
- Prefer centralizing auth/token/cookie handling; avoid duplicated parsing logic.
- Do not introduce browser-readable secrets unless explicitly required.
- Normalize error handling through shared helpers (no silent catch blocks).
- Avoid destructive operational commands in scripts (no forced reset flows by default).
- Favor configurable env-based credentials over hardcoded values in compose/scripts.

## Before Finishing
- Run build/lint checks for touched apps where feasible.
- Record residual risks explicitly in audit docs when not fully removable now.
